.TH MW-SERVE 1 "2026-06-22" "MemoryWhale" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mw-serve \- serve the MemoryWhale memory store as a local web dashboard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mw-serve
.RI [ --host
.IR addr ]
.RI [ --port
.IR n ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mw-serve
runs a small, dependency-free HTTP server that renders the local MemoryWhale
database as a browsable dashboard: recorded sessions, command runs with their
full command lines, projects grouped by working directory, and an interactive
knowledge graph. It reads the same local SQLite database written by
.BR mw (1)
and
.BR mw-remember (1)
and serves entirely from the local machine.
.PP
On start it self-heals by importing any session transcripts whose recording was
interrupted before its database row was written.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--host " addr
Address to bind. Default
.BR 0.0.0.0 ,
which makes the dashboard reachable from other machines on the LAN (for
example, opening a Jetson's dashboard from a laptop browser). Use
.B 127.0.0.1
to restrict it to localhost.
.TP
.BI "--port " n
TCP port to listen on. Default
.BR 7071 .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Localhost only:
.B mw-serve --host 127.0.0.1
.TP
Reachable on the LAN at port 8080:
.B mw-serve --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8080
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mw (1),
.BR mw-remember (1)
